WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.720
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:12.240
Today we are going to perform something that seems&nbsp;
like a true miracle. Oh yes, you are seeing it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:21.120
correctly. This is robotic telekinesis. Moving&nbsp;
objects from afar. So, what is going on here?

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.800
Well, we take a human operator, who&nbsp;
performs these gestures, which are then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:33.600
transferred to a robot arm, and then,&nbsp;
the magic happens. This is unbelievable!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.680
So now, hold on to your papers, and let’s&nbsp;
see how well it can pull off all this!

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:47.760
Level 1 - Oh my, it comes out guns&nbsp;
blazing! Look at that! It is not a brute,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.840
not at all! With delicate movements,&nbsp;
it can pick up these plush toys, or,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:58.160
even rotate a box. That is a fantastic start.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.040
But, it can do even better!

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:08.560
Level 2 - Let’s try to pick up those scissors.&nbsp;
That is going to require some dexterous hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:15.600
movements from the operator and…wow! Can you&nbsp;
believe that? By the time I am saying this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:22.880
it is already done. And, it can also stack&nbsp;
these cups, which is a difficult matter as its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:30.960
own finger might get in the way. This was a little&nbsp;
more of a close call, but it still managed. Bravo!

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:39.360
So, with all these amazing tasks, what could&nbsp;
possibly be level 3? Well, check this out!

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:45.360
Yes, we are going to attempt to open&nbsp;
this drawer. That is quite a challenge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:51.360
Now note that it is slightly ajar to make&nbsp;
sure the task is not too hard for its fingers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.400
and, let’s see! Oh yeah! Good job little robot!

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:01.920
But what good is opening a drawer&nbsp;
if we aren’t doing anything with it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:09.120
so, here comes +1, the final boss level&nbsp;
- open the drawer, and pick up the cup.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:17.920
There is no way that this is possible through&nbsp;
telekinesis. And…oh my goodness. I love it.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:24.320
And note that this human has done&nbsp;
extremely well with the hand motions, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:31.600
is this person a robot whisperer, or can anyone&nbsp;
pull this off? That is what I would like to know.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.920
And, wow! This works with other operators too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:42.560
which is good news, because this means that&nbsp;
it is relatively easy and intuitive to use.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:50.160
So much so, and get this, that these people&nbsp;
are completely untrained operators. So cool!

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:56.080
So, now is the part where we expect the bad&nbsp;
news to come. So, where is the catch? Maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:01.520
we need some sinfully expensive camera gear to&nbsp;
look at our hand to make all this happen, right?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.680
Well, if you have been holding on to your&nbsp;
papers so far, now, squeeze those papers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:15.360
because we don’t need to buy anything crazy at&nbsp;
all! What we need is just one, uncalibrated color&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:22.400
camera. Today, this is available in almost&nbsp;
every single household. How cool is that!

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:28.240
So, if it can do that, all we need is&nbsp;
a bunch of training footage, right? But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:36.480
wait a second…are you thinking what I am thinking?&nbsp;
If we need just one uncalibrated color camera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:43.840
can it be that? Yes! That is exactly right. We&nbsp;
don’t need to create any training data at all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:49.200
we can just use Youtube videos that&nbsp;
already exist out there in the wild!

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:54.160
In a previous paper, scientists at&nbsp;
DeepMind harnessed the power of Youtube&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.160 --> 00:04:01.200
by having their AI watch humans play games,&nbsp;
and then, they would ask the AI to solve hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:07.920
exploration games and it just ripped through these&nbsp;
levels in Montezuma’s revenge and other games too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:14.480
And here comes the best part - what was even&nbsp;
more surprising there that didn’t just perform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:20.800
an imitation of the teacher, no-no. It&nbsp;
even outperformed its human teacher!

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:27.040
Wow. I wonder if we could somehow do&nbsp;
a variant of that in a future paper?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:34.240
Imagine what good we could do with that. Virtual&nbsp;
surgeries? Any surgeon could perform a life-saving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:41.440
operation on anyone, from anywhere else in&nbsp;
the world? Wow. What a time to be alive! Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:47.520
for that, the success rate needs to be much&nbsp;
closer to a hundred percent here, but still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:55.200
this is incredible progress in AI research. And&nbsp;
of course, you are an experienced Fellow Scholar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:05:00.640
so you don’t forget to apply The First Law&nbsp;
Of Papers here, which says that research&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:07.200
is a process. Do not look at where we are, look&nbsp;
at where we will be two more papers down the line.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:13.520
And two more papers down the line, I bet this&nbsp;
will not only be significantly more accurate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:20.320
but, I would dare to say that even full body&nbsp;
retargeting will be possible. Yes, we could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:26.480
move around, and have a real robot replicate&nbsp;
our movements. Just let the computer graphics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:32.160
people in with their motion capture knowledge,&nbsp;
and this might really become a real thing soon.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:37.840
So, does this get your mind going? What would you&nbsp;
use this for? Let me know in the comments below!

